1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,705
Feed production has six main processes.

2
00:00:02,955 --> 00:00:09,450
To maintain the equipment and troubleshoot problems, you need to know what each one does.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,201
One: intake and cleaning, the first line of defense.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:23,902
Trucks are unloaded, and foreign objects like stones, metal and string are removed.

5
00:00:24,152 --> 00:00:31,450
Dust and fines are separated, and material is sent to the right storage.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,554
Two: dosing and weighing.

7
00:00:34,804 --> 00:00:47,450
Certified scales deliver exact quantities of macro and micro ingredients, within the tolerances of the formulation.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,844
Three: size reduction, or grinding.

9
00:00:51,094 --> 00:01:01,365
Hammer mills bring materials to the required particle size, which matters for mixing, pellet quality and digestibility.

10
00:01:01,615 --> 00:01:10,825
For maintenance, remember: performance depends on hammer condition, sieve integrity and proper air balance.

11
00:01:11,075 --> 00:01:14,450
Inspect hammer wear and sieves regularly.

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,155
Four: mixing.

13
00:01:16,405 --> 00:01:29,450
Dry and liquid components are blended into a homogeneous formula, so that every portion of feed has the intended nutrition.

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,068
Five: compacting, in three stages.

15
00:01:33,318 --> 00:01:40,291
Conditioning adds steam or liquids for the right moisture and temperature.

16
00:01:40,541 --> 00:01:45,561
This improves pellet durability and reduces pathogens.

17
00:01:45,811 --> 00:01:56,394
Pelleting forces the mash through a die; die and roller specifications set pellet diameter, length and quality.

18
00:01:56,644 --> 00:02:06,252
Cooling brings pellets to within five degrees of ambient temperature and dries them for safe storage.

19
00:02:06,502 --> 00:02:14,450
Compacting does two jobs: it sanitizes through heat, and it makes a durable product.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,761
Six: finished products.

21
00:02:18,011 --> 00:02:27,450
Feed is bagged at set weights, or loaded onto trucks in bulk for dispatch.

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:45,962
Intake, dosing, grinding, mixing, compacting, and finished products: six processes, one chain.

23
00:02:46,212 --> 00:02:49,450
Now take the quiz.

